// Naive schedule for example 26-bin-min (TASK-0343.01.02).
//
// Single worker `host`, every kernel placed there. The language-sanity
// slice: smoke test that the algorithm parses, lowers, and emits
// bit-identical bytes against `reference.bin`. Even in the single-
// worker path the `result` accumulator must pre-init to the MIN
// identity `i32::MAX` (NOT zero) for the min-fold to be correct — so
// this cell already exercises the identity-aware init on the single-
// worker emit path. No `transfer` directives (no cross-worker edges)
// and no loop transforms — the distributed schedule
// (schedules/distributed.sched.nuc) is where the partition-axis
// MIN-combine actually flexes.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_key    on host;
    place load_val    on host;
    place save_output on host;
    place bin_min     on host;

    // No loop transforms.
    // No transfer directives — no cross-worker edges.
}
